sn4.25:16.1 starts: “How does a monk here often dwell,
sn4.25:16.2 starts: and also the sixth?
sn4.25:16.3 starts: How, while cultivating jhāna,
sn4.25:16.4 starts: does he keep perceptions of sensuality far away?”
sn5.4:5.1 starts: I’m disgusted, ashamed
sn5.4:5.2 starts: of this putrid body—
sn5.4:5.3 starts: disintegrating, dissolving.
sn5.4:5.4 starts: Sensual craving
sn5.5:4.1 starts: “If even a hundred-thousand rapists
sn5.5:4.2 starts: came across me like this,
sn5.5:4.3 starts: I wouldn’t stir a hair.
sn5.5:4.4 starts: and I’m not afraid of you, Māra,
